# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CONVENTIONAL COMMIT MESSAGE TEMPLATE
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Format: <type>(<scope>): <subject>
#
# Types:
#   feat     - A new feature
#   fix      - A bug fix
#   docs     - Documentation only changes
#   style    - Formatting, missing semicolons, etc. (no logic change)
#   refactor - Code restructuring without feature or fix
#   perf     - A code change that improves performance
#   test     - Adding or correcting tests
#   chore    - Build process, tooling, dependency updates
#   ci       - CI/CD pipeline changes
#   revert   - Reverts a previous commit
#
# Scope (optional): module, file, or area affected
#   e.g.: auth, api, ui, db, config, deps
#
# Subject rules:
#   - Use imperative mood: "add feature" not "added feature"
#   - No capital first letter
#   - No period at the end
#   - Max 72 characters on the first line
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

<type>(<scope>): <subject>

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Body (optional — explain WHY this change is needed, not WHAT it does)
# Wrap lines at 72 characters.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Footer (optional)
# Reference issues: Closes #123, Refs #456
# Breaking changes: BREAKING CHANGE: <description>
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

